{
  "requirement": "A definition glob MUST match a complete full name. `*` MUST match zero or more characters, including dots; all other valid name characters MUST match literally. An empty glob MUST be invalid. Every definition selection MUST use this matching rule, including requirements evidence inputs, CLI definition filters, and the authoring `references` tool, and MUST match against both requirements and named examples.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.references.definition_globs`.\n\n**Matching rule**\n- `src/definition_glob.rs#mod[tests]/fn[wildcard_crosses_dot_segments_and_matches_the_whole_name]` checks complete-name matching. `foo.*.bar` matches `foo.x.bar` and `foo.x.y.bar`, so `*` crosses dots. It rejects both a prefixed name and a suffixed name.\n- The same test checks that other characters match literally. `foo.bar` does not match `fooxbar`. `foo_bar-baz` does not match `fooXbar-baz` or `foo_barXbaz`. `foo.bar.*` does not match `foo.bar`, because the dot is literal.\n- Zero-character `*` is covered through `tests/commands.rs#fn[commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors]`. In it, `status requirements.*ready` selects both `requirements.ready` (zero characters) and `requirements.xready`, and excludes `requirements.pending`.\n\n**Invalid globs**\n- The unit test asserts that `validate(\"\")` and `validate(\"foo[bar]\")` are errors.\n- The evidence test `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirements_inputs_track_matched_declarations_in_full_name_order]` asserts specific errors for `\"\"` (\"definition glob must not be empty\") and for `foo.[a].bar`.\n- `fn[commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors]` checks that `info [` and `status [` fail with \"invalid definition glob\".\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` asserts that `references` rejects `\"\"` and `bad name`.\n- The CLI has no test for an empty glob. I read the implementation only to check whether the CLI shares the validation code. `src/commands.rs` (`status_markdown_with_github` and `info_markdown`) calls the same `definition_glob::validate` as the unit-tested path. A CLI-specific empty-glob test would add little, so I do not count this as a gap.\n\n**Every selection surface, matching requirements and examples**\n- **Evidence inputs:** the requirements-input test uses `foo.*.bar`. It matches the example `foo.a.b.bar` and the requirement `foo.a.bar`, and it checks added, removed and no-match outcomes. `tests/definitions.rs#fn[selections_match_requirements_and_examples_but_never_named_definitions]` also covers this surface.\n- **Authoring `habeas` requirements read:** `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirements_reads_select_requirements_and_examples_but_not_definitions]` shows `requirements.*` returns both `requirements.case` (an example) and `requirements.ready`. It also shows that a named definition matches nothing.\n- **CLI filters:** `tests/definitions.rs#fn[selections_match_requirements_and_examples_but_never_named_definitions]` runs `status rules.*` and `info rules.*`. Both include the requirement and the example, and neither includes the definition. `info rules.used` fails.\n- **`references` tool:** `fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` checks that `requirements.*` yields all definitions, including the example, and 4 sites.\n- **`ripgrep` and `ast_grep` `referencing` selections:** `fn[ripgrep_referencing_searches_only_referencing_files_or_nodes]` and `fn[ast_grep_referencing_restricts_the_search_as_ripgrep_does]` apply globs and check the results.\n\n**Not gaps**\n- Multi-star patterns and zero-length `*` in the middle of a name are not separately tested. They fall in the same input classes already exercised, so I do not count them as gaps.\n- The tests in `tests/commands.rs` named `verbose_status_lists_fixme_judgments_and_globs_scope_issue_groups` and `status_retains_repository_findings_without_indexing_unreferenced_functions` add further CLI coverage of glob scoping.",
  "references": "288667bf2256bfb2c1e3d9a893df50df3abc797b6e7682916392f4e0759318ed",
